# The tool images scripts/check.sh runs, each pinned by digest: a tag can be
# moved upstream (or hijacked), a digest cannot, so what checks the house's
# code changes only when this file does. Each digest is the multi-arch index,
# so the same pin works on x86 and on a Pi.
#
# To bump one: pick a release at least two weeks old (a bad release is usually
# pulled within days), `docker pull <image>:<tag>`, copy the "Digest:" line it
# prints, and update the comment beside it. Then run scripts/check.sh full and
# scripts/check.sh vuln once by hand before committing.
#
# Sourced by bash: plain NAME=value lines and comments only.

# shellcheck v0.11.0 (2025-08-04). The version blockyard and the old CI job
# already used, so moving to this kit changes no shell verdict.
SHELLCHECK_IMAGE=koalaman/shellcheck@sha256:61862eba1fcf09a484ebcc6feea46f1782532571a34ed51fedf90dd25f925a8d

# gitleaks v8.30.1 (2026-03-21), the official image. Secrets in commits: the
# PII scan only sees the tree, and a token deleted in a later commit is still
# in history forever.
GITLEAKS_IMAGE=ghcr.io/gitleaks/gitleaks@sha256:c00b6bd0aeb3071cbcb79009cb16a60dd9e0a7c60e2be9ab65d25e6bc8abbb7f

# actionlint 1.7.12 (2026-03-30). Workflow syntax, expressions and runner
# labels; it carries its own shellcheck for run: blocks.
ACTIONLINT_IMAGE=rhysd/actionlint@sha256:b1934ee5f1c509618f2508e6eb47ee0d3520686341fec936f3b79331f9315667

# zizmor 1.30.1 (2026-09-09), the official image; 1.31 was days old when
# pinned. Workflow security: unpinned uses:, persisted checkout credentials,
# template injection, risky triggers. Run with --offline, so it never calls
# GitHub's API.
ZIZMOR_IMAGE=ghcr.io/zizmorcore/zizmor@sha256:a2eb396d886c053073405c7a980f2139ba2248ec172243cfa3841e57196e8101

# hadolint v2.15.1 (2026-07-31). Dockerfiles: unpinned base images and
# packages, the mistakes that make a rebuild quietly different.
HADOLINT_IMAGE=hadolint/hadolint@sha256:32dac94127fd60b7b7e3fbfc65e1383b9b5e25c9bfd7b8536de7a539fe68a12d

# trivy 0.75.0 (2026-10-01); 0.76 was days old when pinned. Known
# vulnerabilities in lockfiles and images. The scan runs with no network:
# only the database download reaches out, and that container never sees the
# repo.
TRIVY_IMAGE=aquasec/trivy@sha256:af6acf9a6b85dfe389a1941505c0ce9efef52a4719635e1a962f022a3d855daa
